TensorFold 0.6.1 (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold, revision
17c73e189f5e6a5304cda7ea37f086f9c49b4788), Apache License, Version 2.0

Two ideas of TensorFold 0.6.1's "Flash Next on Macs at long context" (commit
b8027439) are reimplemented in src/mlx2/runtime/models/qwen4_qsa_scores.py
(block scores that read each pooled block once for every query row) and in
src/mlx2/runtime/models/qwen4_exp.py (the layers before the n-gram layer are
dispatched before it reads a window's ids on the host). No TensorFold source
is copied; the arithmetic is MLX's. See
provenance/tensorfold-0.6.1-flashnext-longctx.json. TensorFold's NOTICE file
reads:

